{"step_index":81,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T06:35:48Z","content":"Awesome! Your GitHub credential is now encrypted with AES-256 and safely stored in your browser's IndexedDB.\n\nHere is how you use it:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Copy Password to Clipboard (Fastest Way)\n* Look at the **Password** line on your GitHub card:\n  ```text\n  Password   ••••••••••••   👁   📋\n  ```\n* Click the **Copy button (📋)** next to the eye icon. \n* A notification will pop up: *\"Password copied to clipboard!\"*.\n* Now simply go to GitHub and press **`Ctrl + V`** to paste it into the password box!\n\n---\n\n### 2. View / Reveal the Password\n* Click the **Eye icon (👁)** on that line to toggle between the hidden dots (`••••••••••••`) and the actual plain text password.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Copy Your Username\n* Click the **Copy button (📋)** next to `vijay@gmail.com` to copy your email/username without needing to type it manually.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Jump Straight to the Website\n* Click **`github.com ↗`** underneath the GitHub title to open GitHub directly in a new tab.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Check the Red \"Health (1)\" Alert (Top Bar)\nNotice the **`Health 1`** badge in your top header:\n* Click on **Health** — the vault scans your passwords locally and flags if a password is weak (under 12 characters) or reused.\n* You can click **\"✨ Generator\"** in the top bar anytime to generate an unbreakable 20+ character password for your accounts!\n\n---\n\n### 6. When You're Done: Lock the Vault\n* Click the red **`🔒 Lock`** button in the top right. \n* This immediately purges the master encryption key from memory so no one else using your computer can see your passwords without entering the master password again.","thinking":"**Observing Vault Item Details**\n\nThe user has successfully unlocked the vault. An item labeled `github` is now visible within the vault, containing a link, username, and obscured password. The presence of the unlocked vault and the displayed credentials indicates successful access.\n\n\n"}
