{"step_index":117,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T06:57:24Z","thinking":"**Determining Project Run Instructions**\n\nUnderstand the user needs VS Code run instructions. The request mentions two distinct projects. One is a web app, the other a browser extension. Each requires a different approach to \"running\" them in VS Code. I'll need to figure out the general steps for each project.\n\n\n**Outlining VS Code Run Instructions**\n\nDelineated instructions for the React web app and the browser extension. The web app requires opening a folder, installing dependencies and running the development server and then opening the URL.\n\nFor the browser extension, the steps include opening the appropriate project folder. I believe the extension would benefit from a `.vscode/launch.json` configuration for easier debugging and development.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"{\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.2.0\\\",\\n  \\\"configurations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Launch Chrome with Extension\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"chrome\\\",\\n      \\\"request\\\": \\\"launch\\\",\\n      \\\"runtimeArgs\\\": [\\n        \\\"--load-extension=${workspaceFolder}\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/login\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Launch Edge with Extension\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"msedge\\\",\\n      \\\"request\\\": \\\"launch\\\",\\n      \\\"runtimeArgs\\\": [\\n        \\\"--load-extension=${workspaceFolder}\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/login\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"","Description":"\"Create VS Code launch.json for one-click browser extension debugging\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\vijay\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\offline-vault-extension\\\\.vscode\\\\launch.json\"","toolAction":"\"Creating launch.json for extension\"","toolSummary":"\"Create VS Code launch.json for extension\""}}]}
