{"step_index":121,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T07:00:18Z","content":"The reason for this error is that you are inside the **`offline-vault-extension`** folder. \n\nA **Browser Extension does NOT need `npm`** — it runs directly inside Chrome or Edge without installing any packages!\n\n---\n\n### If you want to run the Browser Extension:\n\nYou don't need to type any terminal commands. Just do this:\n\n1. Press **`F5`** on your keyboard in VS Code.\n2. Select **\"Launch Chrome with Extension\"** (or Edge).\n3. VS Code will automatically open a browser window with your extension already installed!\n\n*(Alternatively, open Chrome > go to `chrome://extensions` > turn on Developer mode > click **Load unpacked** > select this folder).*\n\n---\n\n### If you wanted to run the Web App:\n\nThe `package.json` file is in the `offline-password-manager` folder. Run this command in your VS Code terminal to switch to it:\n\n```powershell\ncd ..\\offline-password-manager\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```","thinking":"**Diagnosing \"ENOENT\" Error**\n\nThe error message indicates an \"ENOENT\" error, specifically related to `package.json`. This implies the system cannot locate the `package.json` file in the specified directory, a potential file path issue or missing file. The current directory appears correct, which suggests a possible issue with the file's presence or accessibility within the directory.\n\n\n"}
