{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T07:18:06Z","content":"Great job! \n\nNow let’s do the final two steps to see everything come together:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Update the GitHub Password to Clear the Warning\n1. In the **Generator**, click **\"📋 Copy Password\"** (or click Done).\n2. On your GitHub card on the screen, click the **Pencil icon (✏️)** to edit it.\n3. Paste (`Ctrl + V`) your new strong password into the Password field.\n4. Click **\"Save Changes\"**.\n5. Look at the top bar: the red **`Health 1`** alert will disappear, and your vault is now 100% secure!\n\n---\n\n### 2. Test the 1-Click Auto-Fill on GitHub!\nNow let's test the browser extension you loaded:\n\n1. Open a new tab and go to **https://github.com/login**.\n2. Click the **🛡️ Offline Vault** icon in your browser toolbar (click the puzzle piece icon at the top right of Chrome to pin it if needed).\n3. If you see your GitHub entry listed with a **\"⚡ Fill on Tab\"** button:\n   - Click **\"⚡ Fill on Tab\"**!\n   - Your username and password will instantly be typed into GitHub's login boxes automatically!\n4. You will also see a small **green shield icon (🛡️)** right inside the login fields on GitHub that you can click anytime to auto-fill."}
