{"step_index":131,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:19:38Z","content":"Awesome! Your new credential is now encrypted locally with AES-256 and safely stored in your offline vault.\n\nHere are a few cool things you can try with your new password right now:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Test Instant Search\n* Click on the **Search bar** at the top (`Search logins, cards, notes...`).\n* Type the first 2 or 3 letters of your new entry — watch how the vault instantly filters your cards in real time!\n\n---\n\n### 2. Mark as Favorite\n* Click the **Star icon (☆)** on your new card.\n* Now click **\"Favorites\"** in the left sidebar — it will filter down to only your starred accounts for quick access!\n\n---\n\n### 3. Test the Auto-Fill on that Website\n* If you saved a website URL for that entry (e.g. `google.com`, `netflix.com`, etc.):\n  1. Open that website's login page in another tab.\n  2. Click the **🛡️ Offline Vault** extension icon in your browser toolbar (or click the shield icon inside the login box).\n  3. Click **\"⚡ Fill on Tab\"** to watch it auto-fill your credentials in 1 click!\n\n---\n\n### 4. Test Locking the Vault\n* Click the red **`🔒 Lock`** button in the top right.\n* Notice that all passwords are immediately flushed from memory. \n* Type your master password to unlock and verify that all your saved credentials are still there, safe and encrypted!","thinking":"**Confirming Successful Password Addition**\n\nThe user reports adding a new password after following setup steps and exploring other features. It's likely they are signaling successful completion of a core function. Further assessment might be warranted to confirm if the user's workflow is now aligned with desired operation.\n\n\n"}
